hadiths[117]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1312","[AI-translation] He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Live as long as you wish, for indeed you will die. Love whomever you wish, for indeed you will part with him. Do whatever you wish, for indeed you will be recompensed for it. And know that the honor of the believer is his standing in the night, and his dignity is his independence from the people."
"1313","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, said: Do you know who the bankrupt is? They said: The bankrupt among us is the one who has neither a dirham nor any goods. He said: The bankrupt of my Ummah comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and Zakah, but comes having insulted this one, falsely accused this one, consumed the wealth of this one, shed the blood of this one, and struck this one. So this one is given from his good deeds, and this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds are exhausted before what is due upon him is fulfilled, some of their sins are taken and cast upon him, then he is cast into the Fire."
"1314","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Leave me as I leave you. For when I narrate to you, take from me. Verily, those before you were destroyed due to their excessive questioning and differing with their prophets."
"1315","[AI-translation] From Ibn Tawus, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, appointed 'Ubadah bin Al-Samit over the Sadaqah. Then he said to him: ""Fear, O Abu Al-Walid, lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel on your neck that is grumbling, or a cow that is mooing, or a sheep that is bleating."
"1316","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, said: Beware of oppression, for oppression is darkness on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of stinginess, for stinginess destroyed those before you, leading them to shed their blood and make lawful their sacred things."
"1317","[AI-translation] From Sahl bin Abi Hathmah who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, on the pulpit saying: Avoid the seven major sins. The people fell silent and no one spoke. He said: ""Will you not ask me about them? They are: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, fleeing from the battlefield, consuming the wealth of an orphan, consuming Riba, slandering a chaste woman, and reverting to nomadism after emigration."
"1318","[AI-translation] Nu'man bin Bashir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: Make a barrier of the lawful between you and the unlawful. Whoever does that seeks to protect his religion and his honor. And whoever grazes around it is like one who grazes near a protected pasture, destined to soon stumble into it."
"1319","[AI-translation] From Fadalah bin 'Ubayd, the Prophet said: ""Make a barrier between yourselves and the Fire, even if it be with half a date."
"1320","[AI-translation] Hubrani who said: Abu Umamah Al-Bahili took me by the hand and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) took me by the hand and said to me: ""O Abu Umamah! Among the believers are those whose hearts soften for me."
"1321","[AI-translation] From Anas, the Prophet said: ""When Allah intends good for a servant, He hastens his punishment in this world. And when Allah intends evil for a servant, He withholds his sins until he meets Him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1322","[AI-translation] Hamq Al-Khuza'i, the Prophet said: ""When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a servant, He sweetens him."" It was said: ""And what is His sweetening of him?"" He said: ""He opens for him a righteous deed before his death until He is pleased with him concerning his state."
"1323","Al-'Aizar ibn Jarwal al-Hadrami said: There was a man among us called Abu Umayr. He was a brother (in faith) to Abdullah—meaning Ibn Mas'ud. Abdullah used to visit him at his home. He came once but did not find him at home, so he entered upon his wife. While he was with her, she sent her servant on an errand. The servant was delayed, so she said: ""You have delayed, may Allah curse you!"" Abdullah then left and sat at the door. Abu Umayr came and said to Abdullah: ""Why did you not enter upon your brother's family?"" He said: ""I did, but she sent the servant on an errand, the servant delayed, so she cursed her. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When a curse leaves the mouth of its utterer, it looks; if it finds a path to the one it was directed at, [it proceeds], otherwise it returns to the one it came from. And I disliked being a path for the curse.'"""
"1324","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, the Prophet said: ""When you see Allah giving the servant from the worldly life what he loves despite his disobedience, then it is only a gradual enticement."" Then he recited: [Al-An'am] ""So when they forgot that by which they had been reminded, We opened to them the doors of every thing until, when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them by surprise, and at once they were in despair."" (44)"
"1325","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr who said: While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), he mentioned the trials, or it was mentioned in his presence. He said: ""When you see the people's covenants becoming loose and their trusts diminishing, and they are like this,"" and he intertwined his fingers. The narrator said: I stood up to him and said: ""How should I act at that time, may Allah make me your ransom?"" He said: ""Stay in your house, control your tongue, take what you know and leave what you reject, and focus on the affairs of your own self and leave the affairs of the general public."
"1326","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr who said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Advise me."" He said: ""When you commit a bad deed, follow it with a good one that will erase it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is 'La ilaha illallah' among the good deeds?"" He said: ""It is the best of good deeds."
"1327","[AI-translation] 'As, the Prophet said: ""Four traits, if they are in you, then what you missed of the world will not harm you: preserving a trust, truthful speech, good character, and chastity in eating."
"1328","[AI-translation] From Anas, the Prophet said: ""Do good all your lives, and expose yourselves to the breezes of the mercy of Allah, for Allah has breezes of His mercy with which He touches whomever He wills of His servants. And ask Allah to conceal your faults and to secure your fears."
"1329","[AI-translation] Bahili, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee Paradise for you: when any of you speaks, let him not lie; when he is trusted, let him not betray; when he promises, let him not break it; lower your gazes, restrain your hands, and guard your private parts."
"1330","[AI-translation] Anas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best among you? The best among you are those with the longest lifespans, provided they act rightly."
"1331","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Sa'id (marfu'an): ""O Allah, cause me to live poor, cause me to die poor, and resurrect me among the company of the poor."
"1332","[AI-translation] 'As said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, saying openly, not secretly: ""The family of Abu Fulan are not my allies; my ally is but Allah and the righteous believers."
"1333","[AI-translation] 'Aishah said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, when Allah sends down His might upon the people of the earth while the righteous are among them, will they perish with their destruction?"" He replied: ""When Allah sends down His might upon the people of His wrath while the righteous are among them, they are afflicted along with them, then they are resurrected according to their intentions."
"1334","[AI-translation] Narrated from one of the Banu Sulaym who said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, tests His servant by what He gives him. Whoever is pleased with what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has apportioned for him, Allah blesses it for him and expands it, and whoever is not pleased, it is not blessed for him."
"1335","[AI-translation] Abu Umamah said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: ""What do you think of a man who fights seeking reward and fame, what does he get?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Nothing for him."" He repeated it three times, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, kept saying to him: ""Nothing for him."" Then he said: ""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept any deed except that which is purely for His sake and by which His Face is sought."
"1336","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Allah says: 'O son of Adam, free yourself for My worship, I will fill your chest with richness and block your poverty. But if you do not do so, I will fill your hands with preoccupation and not block your poverty.'"
"1337","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah (marfu'an): ""The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is that it will be said to him: 'Did I not make your body healthy for you, and give you cold water to drink?'"
"1338","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah (marfu'an): ""My allies on the Day of Resurrection are the pious, even if one's lineage is closer than another's. So do not let the people come to me with deeds while you come to me carrying the worldly life upon your necks, and you say: 'O Muhammad!' So I will say like this and like this: 'No,' and I will turn away on both sides."
"1339","[AI-translation] Darda' said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""There lies ahead of you a steep mountain pass; none shall cross it save those who are lightly burdened."
"1340","[AI-translation] From Anas: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was mentioned to us as saying: There are among you a people who worship until they amaze the people and amaze themselves, yet they pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game."
"1341","[AI-translation] From Aisha, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: If you have committed a sin, seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him, for indeed repentance from the sin is regret and seeking forgiveness."
"1342","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, marfu'an: Allah has certain people whom He singles out with blessings for the benefit of the servants, and He keeps them in them as long as they bestow them. But if they withhold them, He takes them away from them and transfers them to others."
"1343","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, marfu'an: Indeed Allah has servants who know people by insight."
"1344","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed Allah hates obscenity and lewd speech. And by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not be established until the trustworthy is betrayed and the treacherous is trusted, until obscenity and lewdness become widespread, the severing of family ties, and bad neighborliness. Indeed the parable of the believer is like that of a piece of gold: its owner puts it in the fire (to test it), yet it neither changes nor loses weight. And by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muḥammad, indeed the parable of the believer is like that of the bee: it eats what is pure, produces what is pure, and when it lands it neither breaks nor spoils."""
"1345","[AI-translation] From Ubayy bin Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The food of the son of Adam has been struck as a parable for the world. So look at what comes out of the son of Adam, even if he spices it and salts it, he already knows what it will become."
"1346","[AI-translation] From Fatimah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Among the worst of my ummah are those who were nourished with luxury, those who seek varieties of food and varieties of clothing, and who speak pretentiously."
"1347","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Among people are keys to good, locks for evil. And among people are keys to evil, locks for good. So glad tidings to him whom Allah has made the keys of good upon his hands, and woe to him whom Allah has made the keys of evil upon his hands."
"1348","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik: That the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, used to say while digging the trench: ""We are those who pledged allegiance to Muhammad, upon Jihad as long as we remain forever."" And the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, used to say: ""O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun."" And the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was brought barley bread with rancid fat upon it, and they ate from it. And the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter."
"1349","[AI-translation] And he said, peace be upon him: Only he who is forgiven finds rest. It is narrated from the hadith of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and Bilal al-Habashi, and Muhammad bin Urwah as a mursal hadith."
"1350","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, recited: ""Has there not been over man a period of time, when he was not a thing worth mentioning?"" (Al-Insan) until he finished it. Then he said: I see what you do not see, and I hear what you do not hear. The heaven has creaked, and it has the right to creak. There is no spot in it the size of four fingers except that there is an angel placing his forehead prostrating to Allah. By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would not enjoy yourselves with women upon the beds, and you would go out to the open roads crying out."
"1351","[AI-translation] Khudri reported that a man came to him and said: ""Advise me."" He replied: ""You have asked about what someone before you asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family. He said: 'I advise you to fear Allah, for it is the head of everything. And upon you is Jihad, for it is the monasticism of Islam. And upon you is the remembrance of Allah and the recitation of the Quran, for it is your spirit in the heaven and your mention on the earth.'"
"1352","[AI-translation] Al-Bara' bin 'Azib said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, he caught sight of a group and said: ""What have these gathered for?"" It was said: ""For a grave they are digging."" He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, was startled, so he rushed ahead of his companions until he reached the grave and knelt over it. He said: I faced him from in front of him to see what he was doing, and he wept until the moist earth was soaked by his tears. Then he turned to us and said: ""O my brothers! Prepare for a day like this."
"1353","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1353 Arabic Hadees:"
"1354","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Which of you loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, there is none of us except that his own wealth is more beloved to him than the wealth of his heir."" He said: ""Know that there is none of you except that the wealth of his heir is more beloved to him than his own wealth. Your wealth is what you have sent forward, and the wealth of your heir is what you have left behind."
"1355","[AI-translation] He said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""Three are destructive, and three are saving."" He said: ""Three are destructive: obeyed stinginess, a followed desire, and a person's self-admiration. And three are saving: fear of Allah in secret and in public, moderation in poverty and wealth, and justice in anger and pleasure."
"1356","[AI-translation] Ansariyya of Banu Najjar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, came to us one day... I brought him a pot containing a loaf of bread or some thick soup. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, put his hand in the pot to eat, but his fingers got burned, so he said: ""Hah!"" Then he said: ""O son of Adam, if cold afflicts him he says: Hah! and if heat afflicts him he says: Hah!"
"1357","[AI-translation] An-Nu'man bin Bashir said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The group is mercy, and division is torment."
"1358","[AI-translation] Hadrami - meaning Shuraih - reported that when death approached Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, he said: ""O people of Ash'ar, let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: 'The sweetness of this world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of this world is the sweetness of the Hereafter.'"
"1359","[AI-translation] A man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah the Exalted said: ""O son of Adam, stand for Me and I will walk to you, and walk to Me and I will run to you."
"1360","[AI-translation] A man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah the Exalted said: ""O son of Adam, stand for Me and I will walk to you, and walk to Me and I will run to you."
"1361","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik reported, elevated to the Prophet: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""O My servant, I am as you think of Me, and I am with you when you remember Me."
"1362","[AI-translation] From Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A man said, ""By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so."" So Allah said, ""Who is this who swears upon Me that I will not forgive so-and-so?! I have indeed forgiven so-and-so and invalidated your deeds."
"1363","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Jibril said to me: If only you had seen me while I was taking mud from the sea and thrusting it into the mouth of Pharaoh, lest the mercy reach him."
"1364","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: Being slain patiently does not pass by a sin except that it erases it."
"1365","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunayf, from his father, raised to the Prophet: He used to come to the weak among the Muslims, visit them, visit their sick, and attend their funerals."
"1366","[AI-translation] From Thawban from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said: I will surely know a people from my Ummah coming on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the mountains of Tihamah, white, but Allah will make them scattered dust. Thawban said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us, clarify them to us, lest we be among them while we do not know. He said: They are indeed your brothers and from your skin, and they take from the night as you take, but they are a people who, when they are alone with the prohibitions of Allah, violate them."
"1367","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: You will most certainly follow the traditions of those who came before you, handspan by handspan, cubit by cubit, and arm-length by arm-length, such that if one of them were to enter the hole of a lizard, you would enter it, and such that if one of them were to lie with his mother in the street, you would do so."
"1368","Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Kindi reported from his father: A woman went out during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) intending to pray. A man met her and threw his cloak over her, and he fulfilled his desire from her. She screamed, so he fled. Another man passed by her, and she said: ""That man did such and such to me."" Then she came upon a group of the Emigrants (Muhajirun) and said: ""That man did such and such to me."" They went and seized the man they thought had assaulted her and brought him to her. She said: ""Yes, this is he."" They brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). When he ordered him to be stoned, the man who had actually assaulted her stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I am the one who did it."" He said to her: ""Go, for Allah has forgiven you."" He spoke kindly to the man [who was falsely accused], and said to the man who had assaulted her: ""Stone him."" And he said: ""He has repented a repentance such that if the people of Medina had repented with it, it would have been accepted from them."""
"1369","[AI-translation] From Suraqah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) at al-Ji'ranah but I did not know what to ask him. So I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I fill my watering trough, and I wait for my riding animal to be returned to me, and a beast comes and drinks from it. Is there a reward for me in that?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: In every liver that is parched, there is a reward."
"1370","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: If you were to commit sins until your sins reached the heaven, and then you repented, He would accept your repentance."
"1371","[AI-translation] From Jabir, raised to the Prophet: If the son of Adam were to flee from his provision as he flees from death, his provision would overtake him just as death overtakes him."
"1372","[AI-translation] From Utbah bin Abd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: If a man were dragged on his face from the day he was born to the day he dies of old age in the pleasure of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He would consider it insignificant on the Day of Resurrection."
"1373","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, elevated to the Prophet: ""Were it not that the servants commit sins, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would create a creation that commits sins, then forgive them, and He is the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful."
"1374","[AI-translation] Khattab that he heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Were you to rely upon Allah with true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds; they go forth in the morning hungry and return in the evening full."
"1375","[AI-translation] Ansari, elevated to the Prophet: ""Were it not that you have sins which Allah forgives for you, Allah would bring a people who have sins which He would forgive for them."
"1376","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Were it that you did not err, Allah would bring a people who err, and He would forgive them."
"1377","[AI-translation] From Anas: The Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you, we see within ourselves what we love, but when we return to our families and mix with them, we find fault with ourselves."" The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Were you to remain in the state you are in when you are with me in private, the angels would shake hands with you until they shade you with their wings visibly. But [it is] an hour and an hour."
"1378","[AI-translation] Al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to come out to us in the Suffah while we wore the Hawtakiyyah, and he would say: ""Were you to know what is stored up for you, you would not grieve over what has been taken away from you, and Persia and Rome shall surely be opened for you."
"1379","[AI-translation] Usaydi, elevated to the Prophet: ""Were you to be as you are when you are with me, the angels would shade you with their wings."
"1380","[AI-translation] From Abu Ayyub who said when death approached him: ""I had concealed from you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Were it not that you commit sins, Allah would create a creation that commits sins, and He would forgive them.'"
"1381","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, elevated to the Prophet: ""Were you not to commit sins, Allah would bring a people who commit sins, so that He may forgive them."
"1382","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Were you not to commit sins, I would fear for you something worse than that: self-admiration."
"1383","[AI-translation] From Thawban, marfu': Let one of you take a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a wife who helps him in the matter of the Hereafter."
"1384","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Who among you fasted today?"" Abu Bakr said: ""I did."" He said: ""Who among you visited a sick person today?"" Abu Bakr said: ""I did."" He said: ""Who among you attended a funeral today?"" Abu Bakr said: ""I did."" He said: ""Who among you fed a poor person today?"" Abu Bakr said: ""I did."" Marwan said: It reached me that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""These traits do not gather in a man on a single day except that he enters Paradise."
"1385","[AI-translation] From Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""No two persons love each other for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or in Islam, then they are separated except by a sin committed by one of them."
"1386","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu': That which is little and suffices is better than that which is much and distracts."
"1387","[AI-translation] Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, lay down on a mat, which left marks on his side. When he woke up, I began to rub his side and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, would that you had informed us so that we could spread something for you on the mat?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""What have I to do with the world?! What am I and the world?! My example and the example of the world is only like a rider who took shade under a tree, then departed and left it."
"1388","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: Umar entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side. He said, ""O Prophet of Allah, if only you had taken a softer bed than this?"" He said: ""What have I to do with the world?! My example and the example of the world is only like a rider traveling on a hot day, who took shade under a tree for a part of the day, then departed and left it."
"1389","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""There is no servant except that he has a reputation in the heaven. If his reputation in the heaven is good, he is placed well on the earth, and if his reputation in the heaven is bad, he is placed badly on the earth."
"1390","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, marfu': ""There is no believing servant except that he has a sin he commits habitually from time to time, or a sin he persists in that does not leave him until he departs. The believer was created tested, repentant, and forgetful; when he is reminded, he remembers."
"1391","[AI-translation] From Ali ibn Abi Talib, marfu': ""Of the hearts, there is no heart except that it has a cloud like the cloud of the moon. While the moon is shining, a cloud overtakes it and it darkens; then the cloud clears from it and it shines."
"1392","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: ""The parable of my Ummah is like the parable of the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."" Narrated from the hadith of Anas, Ammar ibn Yasir, Abdullah ibn Umar, Ali ibn Abi Talib, and Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1393","[AI-translation] From Ka'b b. Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The likeness of the believer is like a stalk of grain, the wind bending it once this way and once that way. And the likeness of the hypocrite is like the cedar tree, firm on the ground, until it is uprooted all at once."
"1394","[AI-translation] He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the stalk of grain; it tilts at times and stands upright at times. Reported from the hadith of Anas and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1395","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: The likeness of the believer is the likeness of a palm tree; whatever you take from it of anything, it benefits you."
"1396","[AI-translation] Darda', marfu'an: Whoever removes from the road of the Muslims anything that harms them, Allah writes for him a good deed. And whoever has a good deed written for him with Him, Allah will enter him into Paradise by it."
"1397","[AI-translation] He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to know what he has with Allah, Majestic is His remembrance, let him look at what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has with him. It is reported from the hadith of Anas, Abu Hurayrah, and Samura b. Jundub, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1398","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, marfu'an: Whoever pleases Allah by displeasing the people, Allah will suffice him; and whoever displeases Allah by pleasing the people, Allah will leave him to the people."
"1399","[AI-translation] Zubayr b. al-'Awwam, marfu'an: Whoever among you is able to have a hidden righteous deed, let him do it."
"1400","[AI-translation] He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wakes up secure in his person, sound in his body, and possessing his provision for the day, it is as if the world has been gathered for him in its entirety. It is reported from the hadith of 'Ubaydullah b. Mihisan al-Ansari, Abu al-Darda', Ibn 'Umar, and 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1401","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: Whoever adopts the desert life becomes rough; whoever follows hunting becomes heedless; and whoever approaches the doors of the Sultan is put to trial. And a servant does not increase in nearness to the Sultan except that he increases in distance from Allah."
"1402","[AI-translation] From Anas b. Malik, marfu'an: Part of righteousness is that you keep in touch with your father's friend."
"1403","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': Whoever fears will travel early, and whoever travels early will reach the destination. Verily, the merchandise of Allah is expensive. Verily, the merchandise of Allah is Paradise."
"1404","[AI-translation] From Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever fears will travel early, and whoever travels early will reach the destination. Verily, the merchandise of Allah, the Exalted, is expensive. Verily, the merchandise of Allah is Paradise. The striking one has come, followed by the succeeding one. Death has come with what is in it."
"1405","[AI-translation] From Hubayb, from his uncle, he said: A man among the Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, was told about a man among the Companions of the Prophet that he narrates from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: ""Whoever conceals his Muslim brother in the world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection."" So he traveled to him while he was in Egypt and asked him about the hadith. He said: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Whoever conceals his Muslim brother in the world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.'"" He said: He said: ""And I have heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."
"1406","[AI-translation] From Ammar ibn Yasir, marfu': Whoever has two faces in the world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1407","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu': Whoever has the Hereafter as his concern, Allah will place his wealth in his heart, gather his affairs together, and the world will come to him submissive. And whoever has the world as his concern, Allah will place his poverty before his eyes, scatter his affairs, and nothing of the world will come to him except what has been decreed for him."
"1408","[AI-translation] From Zayd ibn Thabit, marfu': Whoever has the world as his concern, Allah will scatter his affairs, place his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world will come to him except what is written for him. And whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah will gather his affairs together, place his wealth in his heart, and the world will come to him submissive."
"1409","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu': Whoever Allah promises a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him, and whoever He promises a punishment for a deed, He has the choice regarding it."
"1410","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': ""Who will take these words from me and act upon them, or teach someone who will act upon them?"" Abu Hurairah said: I said: ""I, O Messenger of Allah."" So he took my hand and counted five, saying: ""Fear the prohibitions, you will be the most worshipful of people; be content with what Allah has apportioned for you, you will be the richest of people; be good to your neighbor, you will be a believer; love for people what you love for yourself, you will be a Muslim; and do not laugh much, for excessive laughter kills the heart."
"1411","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': People are the children of Adam, and Adam is from dust."
"1412","[AI-translation] Juhani, marfu': ""By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no servant who believes and is steadfast except that he will be entered into Paradise. And I hope that you will not enter it until you take up your dwellings, you and those who are righteous among your offspring, in Paradise. And my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me that He will enter into Paradise from my Ummah seventy thousand without account."
"1413","Handhala al-Usaydi, who was one of the scribes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: Abu Bakr met me and said: ""How are you, O Handhala?"" I said: ""Handhala has become a hypocrite!"" He said: ""Glory be to Allah! What are you saying?"" I said: ""We are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he reminds us of the Fire and Paradise until it is as if we see them with our own eyes. Then when we leave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we attend to our wives, children, and properties, and we forget much."" Abu Bakr said: ""By Allah, we experience the same."" So I and Abu Bakr went until we entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: ""Handhala has become a hypocrite, O Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""And what is that?"" I said: ""We are with you, and you remind us of the Fire and Paradise until it is as if we see them with our own eyes. Then when we leave you, we attend to our wives, children, and properties, and we forget much."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you were to remain upon what you are when you are with me and in remembrance, the angels would shake hands with you on your beds and in your paths. But, O Handhala, an hour and an hour,"" three times."
"1414","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) passed by a dead sheep that its owners had discarded. He said: ""By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, this world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners."
"1415","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, elevated to the Prophet: ""By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, if you did not sin, Allah would take you away and bring a people who sin, seek forgiveness from Allah, and Allah would forgive them."
"1416","[AI-translation] Juhani), who said: We were in a gathering when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) came, with traces of water on his head. Some of us said to him: ""We see you in good spirits today."" He said: ""Yes, and praise be to Allah."" Then the people spoke at length about wealth, so he said: ""There is no harm in wealth for one who is conscious of Allah, and good health for one who is conscious of Allah is better than wealth, and a cheerful soul is part of true bliss."
"1417","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar: When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Hijr, he said to them: ""Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping. If you are not weeping, do not enter upon them, lest what befell them befall you."" (And he covered himself with his cloak while on his mount)."
"1418","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not laugh a lot, for excessive laughter kills the heart."
"1419","[AI-translation] From Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) passed by some of his companions while a boy was in the middle of the road. When his mother saw the riding beasts, she feared for her son that he would be trampled, so she rushed forward, panic-stricken, saying: ""My son! My son!"" and picked up her son. The people said: ""O Prophet of Allah, she would not throw her son into the Fire."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: ""No, by Allah, Allah would not throw His beloved into the Fire."
"1420","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) about this verse: ""And those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful"" (Al-Mu'minun: 60). 'A'ishah said: ""Are they those who drink wine and steal?"" He said: ""No, O daughter of al-Siddiq! Rather, they are those who fast, pray, and give charity, while fearing that it will not be accepted from them. 'It is these who hasten to good deeds' (Al-Mu'minun: 61)."
"1421","[AI-translation] Khawlani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: ""Allah will not cease to plant a plant in this religion, using them in His obedience."
"1422","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, elevated to the Prophet: ""A believer should not humiliate himself."" They said: ""And how does he humiliate himself?"" He said: ""By exposing himself to trials he cannot endure."
"1423","[AI-translation] From Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people, purchase yourselves from Allah with the wealth of Allah. If any of you is too miserly to give his wealth to people, let him begin with himself, and let him give charity to himself, so let him eat and clothe himself from what Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has provided him."
"1424","[AI-translation] and in a narration: He said: I sat with an old man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) in the Mosque of Kufah, and he narrated to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) — or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: O people, repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness, for I repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness one hundred times every day."
"1425","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: O Aishah! Beware of the belittled deeds — and in a wording: sins — for they have from Allah a pursuer."
"1426","Narrated by Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out one day on his mount with his companions walking ahead of him. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Do you permit me to advance to you with a willing heart?"" He said: ""Yes."" So Mu'adh drew near to him and they walked together. Mu'adh said: ""May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! I ask Allah to make our day before your day. Did you see if something happens and we do not see anything — if Allah wills — what deeds should we perform after you?""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) remained silent, then said: ""Jihad in the path of Allah."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What an excellent thing is jihad, and the One who has more power over people than that."" [Mu'adh asked:] ""Fasting and charity?"" He said: ""What an excellent thing is fasting and charity."" Mu'adh mentioned every good deed that a son of Adam can do. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""And guiding people to good is better than that."" He said: ""What is it, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, that guiding people to good is better than that?"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) pointed to his mouth and said: ""Silence except for good."" He said: ""And are we held accountable for what our tongues utter?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) struck Mu'adh's thigh and said: ""O Mu'adh, may your mother lose you! And do people get thrown on their faces in Hell except for what their tongues have uttered?! Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent from evil. Speak good and you will gain, and remain silent from evil and you will be safe."""
"1427","[AI-translation] From Ubad bin Tamim, from his uncle (Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim) raised to the Prophet: O remnants of the Arabs! O remnants of the Arabs! (three times), the most fearful thing I fear for you is showing off and the hidden desire."
"1428","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: The least among my Ummah grants protection on their behalf."
